:51:28Z"},{"number":2414,"title":"Determine whether `redirect_uri` should be an optional token request parameter even when specified in the authorization request","comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-12T15:02:34Z"},{"number":2400,"title":"Implement OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata support","comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-27T17:44:12Z"}],"discussions":[],"latest_release":{"name":"7.8.0","tag":"7.8.0","published_at":"2026-11-03T15:53:15Z","body":"This release introduces the following changes:\r\n\r\n  - A new `SetAllowedDecompressionMethods()` API was introduced in the `System.Net.Http` integration packages to limit the decompression methods they can use when extracting HTTP responses. While not recommended, this new option can be used to mitigate the recent [CVE-2026-111497](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-111497) vulnerability. See https://github.com/openiddict/openiddict-core/issues/2568 for more information (thanks @m3nax! ❤️)\r\n\r\n  - HTTP response payloads are no longer logged by default when encountering an error. A new `EnableSensitivePayloadLogging()` API was added to opt out this new behavior. See https://github.com/openiddict/openiddict-core/issues/2558 for more information (thanks @zengqinglei and @m3nax! ❤️)\r\n\r\n  - All the .NET and third-party dependencies have been updated to their latest version.","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":false,"news":[],"stale":false,"snapshot_at":"2026-11-14T08:50:43Z","history_start":"2026-09-06"}